<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech price deregs may push CPI to 9.5 pct - FinMin.</title>
<headline>Czech price deregs may push CPI to 9.5 pct - FinMin.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech Finance Minister Ivan Kocarnik said on Friday that the price deregulation in the energy and housing sectors may push annual inflation to 9.5 percent by the end of the year.</p>
<p>Annual inflation in 1996 was 8.8 percent. The year-on-year rate for January 1997 was 7.4 percent.</p>
</text>
